From: BernSouls <256335293+BernSouls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:51:31 +0000
Subject: [STAGE5 A1-A5] writer truth: a slot holds a measurement or is ABSENT

No switch: these are writer corrections.  What changes in a graph is listed
slot by slot in diagnostics/REPORT.md, stage 5.

orchestration/binder.py
  A1  CURVE_CONTAINMENT.scale_ratio is the log2 ratio of the two footprint
      extents (half-diameter of the positioned member anchors), or ABSENT
      when either end has no extent.  CO_LOCATED.scale_ratio stays ABSENT
      (both detections are pooled over one anchor); the reason is stated at
      the writer.  Detection.scale is not touched.
  A2  the parent of a containment relation is located at the centroid of
      its footprint, not at the first member's anchor; a whole with one
      member has no internal geometry (all three slots ABSENT); the bearing
      of a zero separation is ABSENT.  The edge is still emitted.
  A3  _containment_geometry returns the unit table's quantisation of the
      same values (UNKNOWN where absent) instead of the neutral triple
      (0, 0, 4); the discarded call in _run_curve_containment is removed.

core/schema.py
  A4  EDGE_SCHEMAS names the three membership flags and
      ORIENTATION_CONTINUITY.polarity_rel "categorical", as the unit table
      does.  edge_table_disagreements() joins verify_schema_consistency.
      The level counts of the three flags still differ (8 against 2) on
      purpose: edge_table_level_mismatches(), pinned.  No range, no bin and
      no reader's output changes.

lenses/chain_lens.py
  A5  PEAK_CHAIN writes the closure axis of its population layout (one-hot
      on its two levels): four axes of four.

The CurveComplex lens (lenses/v4.py) is NOT changed: the pre-registered fix
of its link filter failed its own criterion (REPORT.md, stage 5).

Pins: tests_matcher/test_stage5_writer_truth.py.
